<b><b>1st Striking Force 3rd Section (1YB3H)
 </b>BATDIV 2: Battleships Yamashiro, Fusou
 Ad-Hoc Formation: Aviation Cruiser Mogami, Destroyer Shigure
 DESDIV 4: Destroyers Yamagumo, Asagumo, Michishio</b>

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:43.900
<b><b>2nd Striking Force (2YB)
 </b>CRUDIV 21: Heavy Cruisers Nachi, Ashigara
 DESRON 1: Light Cruiser Abukuma
 DESDIV 7: Destroyers Akebono, Ushio
 DESDIV 18:   Shiranui, Kasumi</b>

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.190
<i>As for the fleet as a whole...</i>

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:44.200
<i>reorganization or no, this fleet 
is practically everything we have left.</i>

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:48.990
<b><b>1st Striking Force 3rd Section (1YB3H)
 </b>BATDIV 2: Battleships Yamashiro, Fusou
 Ad-Hoc Formation: Aviation Cruiser Mogami, Destroyer Shigure
 DESDIV 4: Destroyers Yamagumo, Asagumo, Michishio</b>

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:48.290
<i>But the way we're organized...</i>

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.210
1YB3H...

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.180
Shigure, we're together, huh?

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.050
Mogami?

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.150
Yeah. Glad to be working with you.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.390
Me, too.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.450
Let's hurry. Everybody else 
is already together.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:03.270
Yeah.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.410
<b></b>1st Striking Force 
3rd Section

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.630
1st Striking Force, 3rd Section.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:23.660
This is the spot!

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.770
Mogami-class aviation cruiser, Mogami.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.800
Shiratsuyu-class destroyer, Shigure.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.720
Come in.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.300
Excuse us.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.550
You're late! Where have you been?!

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:42.560
Sorry, Yamashiro. I...

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.780
Shigure, I don't need excuses.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:46.470
You're always like this!

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:48.370
Listen up, we're—

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.650
Yamashiro, that's enough.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:57.180
From now on, we're in the same 
fleet. We'll be comrades.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.320
Sister!

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.180
It's important to set 
the right tone from the start!

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:04.330
I can't have a mere destroyer thinking 
it's okay to disrespect me!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:08.310
I'm this fleet's flagship, and I have 
a responsibility to you, too, Sister.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:12.230
You <i>do</i> understand the situation 
the fleet's in, right?!

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.400
Yamashiro...

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:14.860
Now, now...

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.650
What was that, you useless half-cruiser?!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:18.720
What did you call me?!

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.650
And <i>you</i>, Shigure!

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.720
You're always spacing out like that, 
which is <i>exactly</i> why you're all alone!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.030
You're the only one left out of 
the 27th Destroyer Division, right?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.770
W-What? Got a problem?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:35.610
I... I'm the flagship here!

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.380
Oh, jeez...

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:40.200
This fleet's a mess, and 
we haven't even set sail yet.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.200
That sure is a problem.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.830
Well, Miss Flagship, care to elaborate on 
what you meant by "a mere destroyer"?

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.210
Explain.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.960
Well, I didn't mean...

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.440
Yamashiro, you might call me 
a half-cruiser, but actually...

00:10:58.440 --> 00:10:59.630
This is a waste of time.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.440
Explain yourself, c'mon!

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.970
Um, I...

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.380
I said explain.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.570
You see, my flight deck is...

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.360
Yamashiro, everyone.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.230
Why don't we have tea?

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.460
I brought mikan oranges.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.350
What's going on here?

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:30.540
We're setting sail earlier than 
the original plan called for?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.740
That's right.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:33.120
No one told me that!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:34.630
Here, drink.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.360
I got word via encrypted message 
from Yamashiro in Lingga.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:39.630
This is the new plan.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.870
Okay... Thanks.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.140
So, what's the Admiral say?

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.890
Yamashiro, I'll put your tea 
and mikan orange here.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.650
I'm so unlucky...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.660
This is actually pretty good.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.540
Wow!

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.540
One more time! Do it one more time!

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.810
Shigure, thanks for your help back there.

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.920
For helping Yamashiro.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.550
No, I didn't do anything...

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:30.700
We're 1st Striking Force, 3rd Section.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.550
I'm so unlucky...

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:45.070
Our fleet designation is 1YB3H.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:55.080
This mission will likely be
1YB3H's first, and last.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.830
Why?

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:01.190
Shigure, the enemy... 
The enemy is very strong.

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:05.310
Please protect everyone, 
Yamashiro especially.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.980
Of course... Of course I will.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.850
But why is this our last mission?

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:14.350
Shigure, that's because...

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.600
That's because...

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:19.340
It's because...

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:23.110
We're actually a diversionary fleet.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.110
Listen to me, Shigure.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:32.040
We, 1YB3H, are a bunch 
of useless failures,

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:36.000
brought together for a diversion 
that's a suicide mission!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:55.530
Failures... brought together for a diversion?

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:56.750
That's right.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.280
No... a suicide mission?

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.160
Yamashiro.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:04.030
Still, I won't let us get wiped out.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.000
Don't worry, Sister.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.330
As flagship, I'll work with the admiral 
to get prepared as best I can.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:15.040
Don't worry. They're our admiral. 
They've always been with us.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.800
I won't let the others 
call us useless failures!

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.550
We're Battleship Division 2—

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:25.050
We're 1st Striking Force,
 3rd Section, Yamashiro.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:32.680
That's right. We, 1YB3H...

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.310
We won't sink.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.110
We'll come back safe.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:42.200
Shigure.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.690
You bratty little girl.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:15:00.590
And when I've done what I set out to do,

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:10.350
I'll return home, one of these days.

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:20.240
1st Striking Force, 3rd Section, 1YB3H,

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:24.350
will set off tomorrow morning
 for our sortie point of Brunei!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.960
Hurry up and get ready!

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:33.920
Roger!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.630
That goes over here!

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.500
I'll get the amphibious tanks ready, too!

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:44.130
Another encrypted message 
from Yamashiro in Lingga.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.390
They're at the sortie point, right?

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:50.140
Correct. They arrived at Brunei.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.040
Ashigara-san! Nachi-san!

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.710
Calm down. Have some tea first, Abukuma.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.290
Here, take one.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.080
Thank you, Ushio-chan.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.320
Our admiral has given the order!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.280
We're changing part of the plan 
and leaving port now.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.630
So, it's time.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:21.050
Torpedo Squadron 1, ready to go!

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.210
Okay.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:25.050
It's a little early, 
but we'll be heading out.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:26.830
Let's go!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.170
<b>3rd Section</b>

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:44.490
Thanks.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.070
They sure are big...

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:09.840
Yeah.

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:15.040
That's the 1st Striking Force's main fleet.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.220
Yamashiro...

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:19.020
As the diversion,

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:22.840
we'll charge into the strait, 
drawing away the enemy ships

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:26.400
while they strike the enemy's 
ground forces on the island.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.610
They're our primary force.

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:32.080
So, that's the plan. We distract the enemy

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.240
while our big fleet hits 
their forces on the island.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:37.500
That's right.

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.470
I hope they hit 'em hard!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.190
Yeah.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:51.010
Oh, Mogami. Carrier Division 4 
passed me things to give to you.

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:52.900
From Hyuuga-san and the others?

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:53.890
What is it?

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.200
Um, well...

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.080
Those girls...

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:59.480
God, they take up so much space!

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.400
Oh, here it is.

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:07.040
That's a special...

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.220
A Zuiun?

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:11.900
I don't know what they are, 
but they take up too much space!

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.530
Take them off my hands, please!

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.030
They're so cute! Hooray!

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.410
And this, too.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.400
A Kyoufuu Kai seaplane?

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.920
Thank you!

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:29.000
I'll equip them right away!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.650
Thanks, Yamashiro!

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:32.550
That's why you're our flagship, huh?

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:33.360
Quiet.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.670
Our admiral ordered me to give it to you.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:39.170
Get this crap from Carrier 
Division 4 off my hands.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:41.030
Hooray!

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:44.060
What's so great about that junk?

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:48.440
Zuiuns are very good seaplanes. 
I can't equip them, though.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:51.940
I know.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.950
Shigure, protect my sister.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:00.420
Yamashiro?

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.730
Just stay still for a moment, Shigure.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.490
Yamashiro?

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:23.850
Shigure, protect everyone. 
Protect my sister.

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:29.620
Even when I'm gone...

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.800
The operation begins tomorrow.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.870
We weigh anchor at 1530.

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.960
There's still a little time.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.330
Let's get some rest.

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:47.280
Yeah, Yamashiro...

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.450
Let's get a little sleep.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:27.450
Yamashiro, all ships are ready to go.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:30.170
Understood, Sister.

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:36.500
1530. This fleet will now proceed through 
the Surigao Strait and into Leyte!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.160
The 1st Striking Force's main
 fleet has already left.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:45.270
We will support their advance into Leyte Gulf 
and destruction of the enemy invasion force!

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:49.440
1st Striking Force, 3rd Section! 
Weigh anchor!

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:58.910
Orders received. Battleship Division 2, 
